<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5693" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Brĭgantĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, f., or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Brĭgantĭa</span></b> , ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A town in Rhœtia</i>, now <i>Bregenz</i>, <i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 4, 1</span></i> and
			3; Itin. Anton.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Brĭgantīnus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lacus,</span>”
				<i>the lake of Constance</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 17, 29, § 63</span></i>
			 (in <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 2, 8</span></i>, Lacus
			Venetus).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The town of Briançon</i>, <i>in France</i>, <i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 10,
				7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
